      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>As I mentioned in another thread, I&#39;ve been interested in playing around with Fugue State Parse&#39;s logo a bit. &nbsp;I don&#39;t love the design I came up here with as much as the Luminary one I did, but I like it enough and think it&#39;s an improvement over what&#39;s shown on the Kickstarter currently, so I thought I&#39;d share it.</p><p>I tried various ways to incorporate the wall of code we see on her original card&#39;s incap side into the design but found that in just about every case all it did was muddy things up rather than improve it. &nbsp;I finally settled on having it in the background of the top of the card. &nbsp;I think it delivers the wall-of-code effect I was looking for without being too obtrusive back there. &nbsp;It also helps to hide the bad clone stamping I had to do in Photoshop to remove the text from the art available on the Kickstarter. :)</p><p>I also wanted the &quot;fugue state&quot; tag line to focus on the overlapping nature of how I think Parse sees reality now, as if she were Neo viewing the code underlying the world at the same time she views the world itself. &nbsp;That was hard to do without making it unreadable, but I think what I ended up with does what I was looking for well enough.</p><p>I didn&#39;t incorporate arrows into the design at all. &nbsp;That would have felt too literal and I don&#39;t think it needed it.</p><p>Hope you like it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://greaterthangames.com/system/files/forum/attachments/parse%20-%20fugue%20state.jpg\" /></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://greaterthangames.com/system/files/forum/attachments/parse%20-%20fugue%20state%20orig.jpg\" /></p>",
